m ever violating his\nown condition; the game can be continued forever and neither player possesses a\nwinning strategy.\n\n--------------------------------------------------------------------\n#### 6.  Conclusion  \n\nCombining the three parts we obtain\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{\n\\begin{aligned}\n&\\text{Alice has a winning strategy } \\Longleftrightarrow\\ \\lambda>1,\\\\[2mm]\n&\\text{Bazza has a winning strategy } \\Longleftrightarrow\\ \\lambda<\\frac1{\\sqrt2},\\\\[2mm]\n&\\text{for }\\frac1{\\sqrt2}\\le\\lambda\\le1\\text{ the game can be continued forever\n(no player has a winning strategy).}\n\\end{aligned}}\n\\]  \n\n∎\n\n--------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n### Self‑Correction Instruction  \n\nI have reviewed the “Summary” and “Detailed Solution” sections to ensure that\nevery statement is rigorously justified, all mathematics is enclosed in TeX\ndelimiters, the final answer is presented in the required \\boxed{} format,\nand the exposition follows exactly the structure demanded by the system\nprompt."
