urn 2, Bazza chooses x_2 = sqrt{2 - Q_1} = sqrt{2 - λ^2}. So S_2 = λ + sqrt{2 - λ^2}, Q_2 = λ^2 + (2 - λ^2) = 2.\n\nThus after even turn 2, Q_2 = 2 (full bound), S_2 = λ + sqrt{2 - λ^2}.\n\nNow at odd turn 3, Alice chooses x_3 = λ * 3 - S_2 = 3λ - (λ + sqrt{2 - λ^2}) = 2λ - sqrt{2 - λ^2}.\n\nShe must ensure x_3 ≥ 0. For λ > sqrt{2}/2, 2λ > sqrt{2}, so x_3 > 0. For λ = sqrt{2}/2, 2λ = sqrt{2}, so x_3 = sqrt{2} - sqrt{2 - λ^2}. Let's compute λ = sqrt{2}/2, then λ^2 = 1/2, so sqrt{2 - λ^2} = sqrt{2 - 0.5} = sqrt{1.5} ≈ 1.2247. Then x_3 = 2λ - sqrt{2 - λ^2} = sqrt{2} - sqrt{1.5} ≈ 1.4142 - 1.2247 = 0.1895 > 0. So x_3 > 0 for λ = sqrt{2}/2. So Alice can always choose a nonnegative x_3.\n\nNow Q_3 = Q_2 + x_3^2 = 2 + x_3^2.\n\nNow at even turn 4, Bazza chooses x_4 = sqrt{4 - Q_3} = sqrt{4 - (2 + x_3^2)} = sqrt{2 - x_3^2}.\n\nThus x_4 is defined as long as x_3^2 ≤ 2. Since x_3 is at most something, this holds.\n\nNow S_4 = S_3 + x_4 = (S_2 + x_3) + x_4 = (λ + sqrt{2 - λ^2} + x_3) + x_4.\n\nWe can try to see if S_n grows beyond λ n eventually for λ < sqrt{2}/2.\n\nAlternatively, we can try to find a closed form for S_{2k}.\n\nWe can attempt to find a pattern: Under these strategies, after each even turn, Q_{2k} = 2k (full bound). So Q_{2k-1} = 2k-2 + x_{2k-1}^2.\n\nThus x_{2k} = sqrt{2k - Q_{2k-1}} = sqrt{2k - (2k-2 + x_{2k-1}^2)} = sqrt{2 - x_{2k-1}^2}.\n\nThus the recurrence for x_{odd} is:\n\nx_{2k-1} = λ (2k-1) - S_{2k-2}.\n\nBut S_{2k-2} = S_{2k-3} + x_{2k-2}.\n\nWe can try to derive a recurrence for S_{2k} directly.\n\nLet’s denote a_k = S_{2k} (sum after even turn 2k). Then a_0 = 0.\n\nWe have:\n\n- After odd turn 2k+1, S_{2k+1} = a_k + x_{2k+1}.\n\n- x_{2k+1} = λ (2k+1) - a_k.\n\nThus S_{2k+1} = a_k + λ (2k+1) - a_k = λ (2k+1). So after odd turn, the sum is exactly λ (2k+1) (if Alice chooses maximal). So S_{2k+1} = λ (2k+1).\n\n- After even turn 2k+2, x_{2k+2} = sqrt{2(k+1) - Q_{2k+1}}. But Q_{2k+1} = 2k + x_{2k+1}^2 (since Q_{2k} = 2k). So x_{2k+2} = sqrt{2(k+1) - 